Subject: [PATCH 1/8] fix(seo): never emit SVG as og:image/twitter:image;
 validate raster social images

Service detail pages set image to an SVG illustration, so BaseLayout emitted it as
og:image/twitter:image. Social crawlers do not render SVG, so these 6 pages had no
link preview. BaseLayout now falls back to the PNG default (and its alt) when the
requested image is not raster. check-seo-output.mjs now fails on non-raster
og:image/twitter:image so this cannot regress silently (previously it only checked
that the file existed).
